		<added>2026-10-29</added>
		<lastupdated>2026-11-06</lastupdated>
		<name>Battery Monitor Beta</name>
		<summary>Local battery estimates and app usage history</summary>
		<desc>Battery Monitor shows Android's per-app charge estimates, available
foreground/background estimates, wakelocks and the system battery timeline.
It keeps validated usage history on your device, without ads, accounts or
telemetry. Android 14 or later is required.

The History tab shows saved 1-, 7- and 30-day usage and daily app estimates
across charging sessions. Tap a dated bar for its value. Enable Automatic
history or use Capture now to collect readings; missing days stay unknown.
Notification permission is required only for alerts, not local history.
Network permission is used only for temporary ADB setup on this device.

Guided on-device ADB setup grants diagnostic permissions without a computer
or separate Shizuku installation. Keep Android Settings and the app visible
in split screen while pairing. ADB disconnects after setup; Wireless debugging
can then be turned off. Computer ADB and Shizuku remain alternatives.

This early public beta is an independent GPLv3-or-later Wattdog fork;
estimates and physical-device
behavior still need validation. Uninstalling removes saved history.

Setup and limitations: https://github.com/Sivivatu/battery-monitor#install-and-enable-collection
</desc>
